## 2. Non-von Neumann Architectures — In-Memory Computing (IMC / PiM)

### Why IMC matters

| Access type | Energy (per 64-bit word) |
|-------------|--------------------------|
| 8 kB cache | 10 pJ |
| 32 kB cache | 20 pJ |
| 100 MB memory | 100 pJ |
| DRAM | **2,000 pJ (2 nJ)** |
| FP32 multiply | ~5 pJ |
| INT8 multiply | ~0.3 pJ |
| INT4 multiply | ~0.1 pJ |

**Moving a word from DRAM costs ~20,000× more than an INT4 multiply.** This is why IMC matters — by computing where the data sits, you avoid the dominant energy cost.

### Conventional vs Computational Memory (Sebastian et al., Nature)

- **Conventional:** Data flows from memory array → digital interface → ALU. The compute happens in the processor.
- **Computational memory:** Command "perform f on D" goes to the memory; the memory array itself computes f(D) and returns the result.

### IMC Memory Technologies

| Property | RRAM | PCM | STT-MRAM |
|----------|------|-----|----------|
| Mechanism | Filament formation | Phase change | Magnetic spin torque |
| Write speed | ~10 ns | ~50–100 ns | ~2–10 ns |
| Endurance | 10⁶–10¹² | 10⁶–10⁸ | >10¹² |
| Analog (MLC) | Strong | Strong | Limited |
| Maturity | Research/production | Research/early prod | Production (embedded) |

**MLC** = Multi-Level Cell (stores more than 1 bit per cell — needed for analog weights).

### IMC Macro-Categories (Mannocci et al.)

Based on the memristor I-V hysteresis curve:
- **Static IMC (low-voltage regime):** Matrix-vector multiplication, inverse MVM, content-addressable memory, combinatorial optimization, physical unclonable functions, Bayesian inference
- **Dynamic IMC (switching regime):** Supervised training, spike-based learning, stateful logic, true random number generator

### IMC vs non-IMC

From Verma et al. (2019) — IMC enables **~10–1000× gains** in both:
- Normalized throughput (GOP/s/mm²)
- Energy efficiency (TOP/s/W)

### IMC Maturity (TRL 7–8 / 9)

- **Software IMC (DRAM caching/grids):** *Mature* — SAP HANA, Oracle TimesTen, Redis, Apache Ignite. Note: "Software IMC" is keeping the working dataset in RAM instead of on disk — NOT in the circuit sense.
- **Digital CIM (SRAM/PIM silicon):** *Early commercial* — UPMEM PIM-DRAM shipping, Samsung HBM-PIM, Micron CXL DIMMs in trials. INT4/INT8 CIM macros at 22–25 TOPS/W.
- **Analog IMC (memristive/resistive crossbars):** *Pre-commercial* — IBM AIMC prototypes feasible for LLM, Mythic, Aspinity at edge AI stage. Challenges: analog noise, precision limits, scaling.

**Market:** $16.3B (2024) → $46.9B by 2033 at 12.5% CAGR; AI inference is the key growth driver.

### Commercial Products

| Software / Data Platforms | Hardware (PIM/CIM Silicon) |
|---------------------------|----------------------------|
| SAP HANA — #1 enterprise IMC platform | UPMEM PIM-DRAM — 2,500+ processing units on-chip |
| Oracle TimesTen — low-latency OLTP | Samsung HBM-PIM (Aquabolt-XL) — HBM2E + AI engine, 2× BW efficiency |
| Redis — key-value, NoSQL, cache | Micron CXL Memory Expander |
| Apache Ignite / GridGain | Mythic M1076 AMP — analog compute-in-Flash |
| Hazelcast | IBM NorthPole / AIMC chips |
| SingleStore (MemSQL) / VoltDB | Intel Optane PMem (discontinued 2022) |
| Azure Cache / AWS ElastiCache | Everspin MRAM / emerging NVM |

